    {
      "input": "Thanks *he said to them, after which he decides to give them back the boots*\nYou'll need them more than me",
      "outcome": "success",
      "provider_code": null,
      "attempt": 1,
      "prompt_hash": "3e42c4fb394f1653",
      "draft": "Jessa looked down at the leather boots held out toward her, her grey-streaked brow furrowing slightly. She made no move to extend her hands to take them back, leaving them firmly in Nicco's grasp.\n\n\"Keep them,\" she said, her voice measured and quiet amidst the thin daytime traffic of the square. \"Footwear that holds together isn't something to pass off lightly in the West District, and I have no immediate lack of my own. If they fit, wear them. If they don't, find someone who has use for them, but don't hand them back to me.\"\n\nShe rested one hand near the notebook tucked into her belt, her gaze briefly assessing the heavy timber of the massive doorway nearby before settling back on him.",
